# [RXTDUP] rxtnul lane fixture: TWO FILE-LEVEL 'description' LINES.
# docs/spec/rxt_format.md calls this "a machine-readable prose FIELD"
# (singular). Before this fix each occurrence became its own dumped row
# with no cardinality check at all — not the same silent-loss shape as
# the pattern-block case (nothing is overwritten; a second row simply
# appears), but the same author mistake, so it is refused the same way:
# by name, naming the earlier line.
description the first file-level description
description the second file-level description
pattern a+
name one
m "aaa" 0 3
